      "text_with_math_alttext": "We first construct the half-turn process up to an arbitrary time $t$ at fixed $(y,\\widetilde{x})$ in Section A.1. We use an integrated hazard construction [12, Section 2] and prove reversibility by a path reversal argument. We then average over the initial momentum and reference point in Section A.2 to obtain the ideal half-turn kernel and its augmented-space lift. Finally, Section A.3 treats the bounce count at stationarity, the tail behaviour of the event rates, and the implementation via a capped rate.",
