      "raw_fragment_sha256": "de6701cbbba6cbbfc73f8e4de8b4048f1f768f64871ec024b82423ec1cf3be6b",
      "text_with_math_alttext": "Proposition 3.1 (Well-posedness and stationarity of the conditional phase space process). For every fixed $y,\\widetilde{x}\\in\\mathbb{R}^{d}$ and initial phase space point $(x_{0},p_{0})$, the event-driven dynamics in Algorithm 1, with the reference point fixed at $\\widetilde{x}$, defines a unique non-explosive, time-homogeneous Markov process. The phase space measure $\\nu_{\\eta,y}$ is stationary for this process. In particular, the returned position $x_{\\pi}$ is well-defined almost surely.",
